test/check/error-element-each.sumspec:20:31:
   |
20 | targetOnly :: Files -> Files[#p](FileState.Unmodified)
   |                               ^
on the target side, write Files[p]; #p names the key on the source side

test/check/error-element-each.sumspec:22:51:
   |
22 | repeated :: Files[#p](FileState.Staged) -> Files[#p](FileState.Unmodified)
   |                                                   ^
on the target side, write Files[p]; #p names the key on the source side

test/check/error-element-each.sumspec:24:39:
   |
24 | inGuard :: App => Mode.Idle // Files[#p](FileState.Staged) -> Mode.Busy
   |                                       ^
a guard can't pick elements with Files[#p]; write it on the source side

test/check/error-element-each.sumspec:27:48:
   |
27 |   :: App(Files[#p](FileState.Staged) * Others[#q in ps])
   |                                                ^
a transition picks several elements once; Files[#p] already does here

test/check/error-element-each.sumspec:30:12:
   |
30 | notList :: Mode[#m] => Idle -> Busy
   |            ^
Mode is not a list type; [#m] picks elements of a keyed list type, such as L = [T by K]

test/check/error-element-each.sumspec:32:12:
   |
32 | unkeyed :: Sizes[#p](#n) -> Sizes[p](n + 1)
   |            ^
Sizes has no key, so [#p] can't pick elements; declare one, such as Sizes = [Size by Id]

test/check/error-element-each.sumspec:32:29:
   |
32 | unkeyed :: Sizes[#p](#n) -> Sizes[p](n + 1)
   |                             ^
Sizes has no key, so [p] can't pick an element; declare one, such as Sizes = [Size by Id]

test/check/error-element-each.sumspec:34:32:
   |
34 | primed :: Files[#p] -> Files[p]'
   |                                ^
an element takes no prime ('); prime its parts instead, such as Files[x](A')

test/check/error-element-each.sumspec:35:20:
   |
35 | named :: Files[#p]#f -> Files
   |                    ^
an element can't be named yet; name its parts instead

test/check/error-element-each.sumspec:37:24:
   |
37 | twice Path#p :: Files[#p] => FileState.Staged -> FileState.Unmodified
   |                        ^
p is named twice in this transition

test/check/error-element-each.sumspec:39:14:
   |
39 | input Files[#p] :: Mode.Idle -> Mode.Busy
   |              ^
an element path goes on the source or target side, not in the input

